WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.387 --> 00:00:02.970
COLT MCANLIS: This week, we're
talking about the AutoML Tables

00:00:02.970 --> 00:00:06.720
SDK, the new Kubernetes
Benchmark, and Anthos training.

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:09.090
I'm Colt McAnlis, and welcome
to This Week in Cloud,

00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:12.430
where we serve you the
lowest latency news.

00:00:12.430 --> 00:00:15.210
Google Cloud AutoML
offers tools and resources

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:18.540
to help you build the machine
learning models that you need.

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:21.810
And now, the AutoML Tables
SDK brings those tools

00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:24.930
to your own application by
triggering or automating

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:26.400
each step of the process.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.230
Check out this
example, which shows

00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:32.580
how to use the SDK end-to-end
within a Jupyter Notebook.

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:34.590
The Center for Internet
Security provides a set

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:38.260
of Kubernetes security best
practices with their Kubernetes

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:38.760
benchmark.

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:40.900
And the latest version
was just released.

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:44.670
So we've released a new CIS
Google Kubernetes Engine

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:47.430
benchmark to take the guesswork
out of which recommendations

00:00:47.430 --> 00:00:50.460
you should check out and which
ones we've already checked out

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:51.642
for you.

00:00:51.642 --> 00:00:53.350
And when it comes to
keeping you covered,

00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:55.920
we know that customers rely
on Google Cloud Support

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:58.900
to be seamless, simple,
and straightforward.

00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:02.760
So we're adding a new
proactive option to our lineup.

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:05.970
Premium support offers
context-aware experts

00:01:05.970 --> 00:01:08.190
that understand your
architecture and work

00:01:08.190 --> 00:01:10.830
hand-in-hand with your
technical account manager

00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:13.450
to solve your problems.

00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:16.770
Anthos is Google Cloud's
open-application modernization

00:01:16.770 --> 00:01:19.140
platform and can
help your apps become

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:22.870
more portable, maintainable,
scalable, and secure.

00:01:22.870 --> 00:01:25.380
We've just released a new
learning specialization

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:27.960
designed for infrastructure
operators, architects,

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:32.130
and DevOps called Architecting
Hybrid Cloud Infrastructure

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:33.180
with Anthos.

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:33.850
Give it a try.

00:01:33.850 --> 00:01:34.975
Let us know what you think.

00:01:34.975 --> 00:01:37.058
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:37.058 --> 00:01:38.820
or see the full list,
check out the links

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:40.350
in the description and below.

00:01:40.350 --> 00:01:41.560
Any thoughts or ideas?

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:43.230
Leave us a comment
or send us a tweet

00:01:43.230 --> 00:01:45.800
and we'll see you in the cloud.

